-- title:
--   Rank is unchanged modulo a regular element
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative Noetherian local ring and let $M$ be an $R$-module (an additive commutative group with an $R$-module structure) that is finite over $R$, i.e. generated by finitely many elements. Let $x \in R$ lie in the maximal ideal of $R$, assume that $x$ acts regularly on $M$ (multiplication by $x$ is injective on $M$, `IsSMulRegular M x`), and assume that the quotient $M/xM$, written `QuotSMulTop x M`, is a free module over the quotient ring $R/(x)$, where $(x)$ is the ideal `Ideal.span {x}`. Then the finite ranks agree: $$\operatorname{finrank}_{R/(x)}\bigl(M/xM\bigr) = \operatorname{finrank}_R M,$$ the ranks being Mathlib's `Module.finrank`, i.e. the natural number obtained as the cardinality of a basis (and $0$ when no finite basis exists). In particular the equality asserts that $M$ itself has a finite free rank equal to that of $M/xM$ over $R/(x)$.
--
--   This is the rank bookkeeping that accompanies the Nakayama-style lifting of a basis of $M/xM$ to a basis of $M$ for an $M$-regular parameter $x$ in the maximal ideal; it records that reduction modulo such an element does not change the free rank. It is used in the study of multivariate formal groups, in [`MvFormalGroup.finite_free_finrank_quotient_span_nthSeries_of_finrank_eq_pow`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.finite_free_finrank_quotient_span_nthSeries_of_finrank_eq_pow), where ranks of successive quotients have to be compared.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Module_finrank_quotSMulTop_eq.lean

import Mathlib.RingTheory.LocalRing.Module
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.StrongRankCondition
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Regular.IsSMulRegular
